The MongoDB connection is already set up in the server setup section.

### Step 4: Update the patient record with the extracted data

Create a function to update the patient record:

```javascript
async function updatePatientRecord(parsedMessage) {
  const { pid, obx } = parsedMessage;

  if (!pid || !obx) {
    throw new Error('Invalid HL7 message');
  }

  // Extract relevant fields from PID and OBX segments
  const patientId = pid[3]; // PID-3: Patient ID
  const observationData = obx.map(observation => ({
    observationId: observation[3], // OBX-3: Observation ID
    observationValue: observation[5], // OBX-5: Observation Value
    observationUnits: observation[6] // OBX-6: Units
  }));

  // Update the patient record in MongoDB
  const collection = db.collection('patients');
  await collection.updateOne(
    { _id: patientId },
    {
      $setOnInsert: {
        _id: patientId,
        name: pid[5], // PID-5: Patient Name
        birthDate: pid[7] // PID-7: Date of Birth
      },
      $push: {
        observations: observationData
      }
    },
    { upsert: true }
  );
}
```

